  "body": "Small items from the same run:\n- The default post on a wire machine is Fanuc (`posts_with: Fanuc (built-in)`), then refused; MCP cannot set the document's post (set_setup_post only on a declared setup).\n- `edit_operation {\"skims\": []}` is refused (\"unknown field skims\"); `null` works.\n- With skims, the slug report splits one slug into several (7 vs 5 on HolesRow1, small pieces inside the dia-8 hole).\n- A STEP's bottom rim imports with 10 stray 2-edge chains (0.32-0.37 mm) in no loop, easy to mis-pick; `list_features` faces floods (32,614 entries) and truncates.\n- `render_stock` gives no picture for a wire job; verify is text-only.\n- pick_in_box (visible only) also takes rims seen through a through-hole; mixed rims give \"projects to a line from above and bounds no area\"; one closed chain reported length 30.06 vs about 39.6 (a side missing).\n- No tool-steel work material; no new-project tool in MCP.\n\nDone means: each item is fixed or split into its own issue.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
